  "conclusion": "Robustness verified: the construction is 21.9x smaller in real on-wire bytes (16,552 B vs 362,528 B over 300 queries), uses ~20x fewer TCP segments (12 vs 249), and therefore survives packet loss FAR better: at 1% per-segment loss its first-pass success probability is 0.886 vs 0.082 for flat_central, needs 0.12 vs 2.52 expected retransmissions, and completes in 0.0910s vs 0.3408s expected. The construction remains the cheapest AND the most robust mechanism at every tested loss rate (0.5%-10%) on all six metrics (bytes, segments, first-pass success, retransmissions, retransmit latency, completion time)."
